; Expect: Object does not exist
; A variable that still points at a deleted object stops the program when the object is used. Only a debug build (-d) keeps
; deleted objects around to check this, in other builds the memory is free and anything can happen.
If GetEnv$("BLITZLLVM_TEST_DEBUG") = "" Then RuntimeError("Object does not exist (release build, not checked).")
Type MyType
	Field a
End Type
Local a.MyType = New MyType
Local b.MyType = a
Delete a
If a <> Null Then Print "Delete did not set the variable to Null."
Print b\a
Print "A deleted object could be used."
